OL,3,A'No turning back' in independence
OL,4,Ajourney, says first minister at rally
OL,5,
OL,6,FWales' first minister has said there is
OL,7,F"no turning back" on the journey to
OL,8,Findependence for the country, as he
OL,9,Fattended a rally on Saturday.
OL,11,FIn a speech addressing the crowd
OL,12,Fgathered in Aberystwyth, Ceredigion,
OL,13,FRhun ap Iorwerth said the "next step"
OL,14,Ffor Wales had to be "equality with
OL,15,FScotland, as a minimum".
OL,17,FThousands were in attendance, with the
OL,18,Fevent organisers, campaign group Yes
OL,19,FCymru, saying it estimated the march
OL,20,Fattracted between 8,000 and 9,000
OL,21,Fpeople.
OL,23,APub: 26-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG7/39
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
